<!--
  Air-defence gate profile. Mirrors gating.py:_defender_predicates EXACTLY.

  This tree is deliberately SHORTER than the tag profile, and that is the
  finding, not an omission. Measured on `assault` (150 eps x 2 seed blocks,
  DAgger policy on the RL branch), gating one predicate at a time:

      scripted only ............................ 0.54 / 0.56
      InterceptInfeasible -> rl ................ 0.70 / 0.71   <-- shipped
      + ThreatImminent -> rl ................... 0.45 / 0.45
      + DefenderCloseQuarters -> rl ............ 0.12 / 0.12
      rl only .................................. 0.03

  The tag instinct ("close quarters is messy, hand it to the policy") is
  actively harmful here, costing 42 points: the terminal endgame against a
  missile is not a scrappy dogfight, it is a precise geometry problem the
  lead-intercept law solves near-optimally. The one regime worth handing over
  is where the scripted law is not merely imprecise but STRUCTURALLY UNDEFINED
  — no positive intercept root exists, so it falls back to parking on a static
  gate point and has nothing better to offer.

  ThreatImminent / DefenderCloseQuarters stay registered in bt_nodes.cpp so the
  ablation is reproducible from Groot2 by editing this file alone.

  The handover is IMMEDIATE, and that is measured too: debouncing it (fire
  only after k consecutive infeasible ticks) was a clean dose-response loss —
  bt_gated 0.71/0.59/0.49 at perfect link for k=1/2/3, recovering nothing at
  any latency level. Genuine infeasible regimes are 20-30-tick streaks that do
  not flicker; a debounce is pure delay against an 11 m/s missile. Do not
  re-add a persistence threshold without beating that table (details in
  gating.py:_defender_predicates).
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="GateDefenders">
  <BehaviorTree ID="GateDefenders">
    <Fallback name="gate">
      <Sequence name="intercept_infeasible_to_rl">
        <InterceptInfeasible/>
        <SetMode mode="rl"/>
      </Sequence>
      <Sequence name="clean_intercept_to_scripted">
        <CleanInterceptFeasible/>
        <SetMode mode="scripted"/>
      </Sequence>
      <SetMode mode="scripted"/>
    </Fallback>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
